        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2027",
          "width" : 200.3,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 26.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Figure 1: Side view of the test slot with a four-layer spacer under the sliding rail. The dark block is",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 162.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "the spacer; the thin lines mark the slot floor and the rail.",
          "width" : 223,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 173.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Table 1: Measured and predicted heights of folded spacers (mm).",
          "width" : 259.3,
          "x" : 176.3,
          "y" : 206.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Stock Layers Measured Predicted",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 217.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Thin 2 0.46 0.46",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 229.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Thin 4 0.95 0.98",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 240.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Medium 3 1.02 1.00",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 251.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Medium 6 2.05 2.05",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 262
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Thick 4 1.98 1.92",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 273
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "where c is the crease allowance added by each fold. The allowance is found from a two-layer trial,",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 304.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 12.4,
          "text" : "for which Equation (1) gives c = h2− 2t. The same model was used for the gauge block of Scale",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 315.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Fixture Room (2023), where it predicted the height of folded board well for up to four layers.",
          "width" : 371.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 326.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "Card thickness.",
          "width" : 67.6,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 351.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "The thickness t was measured with a dial gauge on ten single sheets of each",
          "width" : 318.5,
          "x" : 185.5,
          "y" : 351.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stock, and the mean was used in the model. The thin stock measured 0.20 mm, the medium stock",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 362.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "0.30 mm and the thick stock 0.45 mm, with a spread of less than 0.01 mm in every case.",
          "width" : 350.2,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 373.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Pressing the crease.",
          "width" : 84.4,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 397.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Every crease was pressed once with the flat of a bone folder along a steel",
          "width" : 301.7,
          "x" : 202.3,
          "y" : 397.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "rule. Pressing twice made the crease allowance smaller but also cracked the surface of the thick",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 409.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stock, so a single pass was used for all spacers.",
          "width" : 187.3,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 420
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "3 RESULTS",
          "width" : 64.3,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 446.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Figure 1 shows the slot with a four-layer spacer in place, and Table 1 lists the mean measured",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 471.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "height of each spacer together with the height predicted by Equation (1).",
          "width" : 288.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 482.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "The model agrees with the measurements to within 0.06 mm for every spacer. The largest error is",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 499.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "for the thick stock, where the crease allowance grows with the number of layers: the outer layers",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 510.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "must bend around a thicker core, and the crease opens slightly. For the thin and medium stocks the",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 521.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "error does not grow with the number of layers, which agrees with the note of Glue Pot Corner",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 532.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "(2022) on thin paper joints.",
          "width" : 108.7,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 543.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Repeated readings of the same spacer differed by at most 0.02 mm. Spacers that were left in the",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 560.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "slot overnight lost about 0.01 mm of height, which is smaller than the spread between readings and",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 571.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "was ignored.",
          "width" : 50.9,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 582.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "4 CONCLUSION",
          "width" : 87.1,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 609.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "A folded card spacer can be designed from the card thickness and a crease allowance measured",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 634.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "once for each stock. For heights up to 2 mm the thin and medium stocks follow the layer model",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 645.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "closely, and they are the better choice when a rail must sit at an exact height. The thick stock is",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 656.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "quicker to fold but should be checked in the slot when more than three layers are used. A card",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 667.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ladder (Window Frame Study, 2021) gives a convenient way to check many spacers at once.",
          "width" : 367.4,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 678.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "2",
          "width" : 5,
          "x" : 303.5,
          "y" : 750.9
        }
